{"id":"fra-t1-0011","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"count.zero","domain":2,"text_native":"zéro","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"None, zero.","source_caption":"0","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Zero is the answer that gets misheard most often, because the word for nothing and the word for a small quantity are often unrelated.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0012","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"price.bill","domain":3,"text_native":"L'addition, s'il vous plaît !","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"The bill, please.","source_caption":"The bill, please!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Where the word for bill and the word for receipt are the same word and neither is 'account'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"687001","author":"atitarev"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0013","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"price.card-ok","domain":3,"text_native":"Acceptez-vous les cartes de crédit?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Is card payment accepted?","source_caption":"Do you accept credit cards?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The alternative to carrying cash, and the question that decides whether you are standing in a queue that moves.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0014","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"price.how-much","domain":3,"text_native":"Combien (ça) coûte?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"How much is this?","source_caption":"How much (is this)?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most useful question in the tier, and the one people are most afraid to ask. It is not rude anywhere.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0015","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-cheap","domain":3,"text_native":"bon marché","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is cheaper in my country.","source_caption":"cheap","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Read as an accusation almost everywhere. Included because knowing that it is an accusation is worth more than being able to say it politely.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0016","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"price.too-expensive","domain":3,"text_native":"C'est trop cher.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"That is too expensive.","source_caption":"That's too expensive.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used with the hand gesture that accompanies it. The gesture carries the meaning and the word confirms it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0017","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"money.atm","domain":3,"text_native":"Où puis-je trouver un distributeur de billets?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is an ATM?","source_caption":"Where can I find a cash point / ATM?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognising rather than producing it: you will be shown the sign rather than expected to ask.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0018","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"money.exchange-rate","domain":3,"text_native":"Quel est le taux de change?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"What is the exchange rate?","source_caption":"What is the exchange rate?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Often answered by pointing at a board rather than spoken.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0019","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"money.keep-change","domain":3,"text_native":"Gardez la monnaie.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please keep the change.","source_caption":"Keep the change.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing loose coins is often faster and always understood.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"2413608","author":"plover"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0020","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"toilet.where","domain":12,"text_native":"Toilettes","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is the toilet?","source_caption":"TOILET","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most urgent question in this tier and the one every phrasebook leads with. In several languages the word is the only one a traveller needs for years.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0021","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"food.delicious","domain":4,"text_native":"Très délicieux !","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is delicious.","source_caption":"Very delicious!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The cheapest goodwill available, and in some of these languages the only correct way to receive a dish rather than simply eat it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"13252168","author":"ntsereteli"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0022","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"food.menu","domain":4,"text_native":"Puis-je jeter un coup d'œil au menu ?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"The menu, please.","source_caption":"Can I have a look at the menu?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"One question covers a whole meal. Most phrasebooks waste slots on individual dishes instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"2794159","author":"mccarras"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0023","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"food.water","domain":4,"text_native":"eau (f.)","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Water, please.","source_caption":"water","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Refusing the water in a restaurant is a small discourtesy in several of these countries. This is how to ask for some instead.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0024","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"way.straight","domain":7,"text_native":"tout droit","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Go straight ahead.","source_caption":"Straight on","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0025","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-left","domain":7,"text_native":"tournez à gauche","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Turn left.","source_caption":"turn left","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced: you are the one being given directions far more often than giving them.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0026","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"way.turn-right","domain":7,"text_native":"tournez à droite","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Turn right.","source_caption":"turn right","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Recognised rather than produced.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0027","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"way.where-to","domain":7,"text_native":"Comment est-ce que je vais à... ?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"How do I get to","source_caption":"How do I get to ...?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Incomplete on its own — a name or a pointing gesture finishes it. That is how it is actually said.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"3217833","author":"lukaszpp"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0028","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"stay.checkout","domain":5,"text_native":"Je voudrais régler la note.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I would like to check out, please.","source_caption":"I want to check out.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said the morning before leaving, so the bill is not waiting at the desk while luggage is being gathered.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0029","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"stay.room","domain":5,"text_native":"J'ai une réservation.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I have a room booked.","source_caption":"I have a reservation.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The opening line at a front desk, and the word that gets you past it is the name on the booking.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"1360227","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0030","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"move.destination","domain":6,"text_native":"Amenez-moi là, je vous prie.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please take me there.","source_caption":"Take me there, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Shown with a map or a written address while saying it. 'There' is the word the pages use; 'this address' is in none of them, and a slot phrased from imagination rather than from a caption is a slot that can never be filled.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0031","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"move.ticket","domain":6,"text_native":"Je voudrais un ticket s'il vous plaît.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"One ticket to","source_caption":"I'd like one ticket, please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Ordering the number and the destination together, which is the whole transaction.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"5288915","author":"mailohilohi"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0032","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"move.where-is-platform","domain":6,"text_native":"À quel quai se trouve-t-il ?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Which platform?","source_caption":"Which platform is it on?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Answered by a sign or a display more often than by a person.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"427558","author":"CM"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0033","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"shop.size","domain":8,"text_native":"Avez-vous une plus petite taille ?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do you have a smaller size?","source_caption":"Do you have a smaller size?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Clothing sizes are not comparable across countries, so asking beats estimating.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"5443276","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0034","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"health.allergy","domain":9,"text_native":"Je suis allergique à...","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I am allergic to","source_caption":"I am allergic to...","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Incomplete until the food or drug is named, which is why it sits beside the food slots.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0035","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"health.doctor","domain":9,"text_native":"J'ai besoin d'un médecin.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I need a doctor.","source_caption":"I need a doctor.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Short enough to say to anyone, which is the point — a phrase you cannot finish is a phrase that arrives too late.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0036","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"health.hospital","domain":9,"text_native":"Où est l'hôpital ?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Where is the nearest hospital?","source_caption":"Where is the hospital?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asked of a passer-by rather than declared to a driver. The pages carry the question and not the instruction to be driven, which is a different conversation with a different person.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba fra-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"3627804","author":"CC"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0037","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"health.hurt","domain":9,"text_native":"Je me suis blessé.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I have been injured.","source_caption":"I've been injured.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Declares the situation before being asked. Several of these languages change tense or register on the word for injury, and the flat version sounds like a complaint.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0038","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"help.dont-touch","domain":10,"text_native":"Ne me touchez pas!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do not touch me.","source_caption":"Don't touch me!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Out loud and to a person, not shouted generally. Several of these languages treat it as an accusation, so it is a sentence to use deliberately.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0039","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"help.emergency","domain":10,"text_native":"C'est urgent!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"It is an emergency.","source_caption":"It's an emergency.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Changes how the next thirty seconds go. Two words, and in several of these languages it reaches a different set of responses than a request would.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0040","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"help.leave-me-alone","domain":10,"text_native":"Laissez-moi tranquille!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please leave me alone.","source_caption":"Leave me alone.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Said firmly and quietly. Raising the volume is what turns it from a boundary into an incident in several of these cultures.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0041","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"help.lost","domain":10,"text_native":"Je me suis perdu(e).","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I am lost.","source_caption":"I'm lost.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Asking a passer-by for help is a separate skill from reading a sign, and it uses different vocabulary in every one of these languages.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0042","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"help.phone","domain":10,"text_native":"Puis-je utiliser votre téléphone?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Can I use your phone?","source_caption":"Can I use your phone?","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The most common thing a traveller needs that a phone provides, and asking a stranger for it is usually granted.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0043","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"help.police","domain":10,"text_native":"Appelez la police.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please call the police.","source_caption":"Call the police.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Usually needs a phone, and in most places a local number rather than an international one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"fra-t1-0044","lang":"fra","tier":1,"slot":"help.thief","domain":10,"text_native":"Arrêtez! Au voleur!","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Stop, thief!","source_caption":"Stop! Thief!","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Loud, and aimed at a crowd rather than at one person. Included because the vocabulary exists and because it is the sentence that makes people nearby move.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: French phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/French_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
